The CEDFrequencyMerger and CEDTemporalMapper definitions and initialization
are retained from Mizar runtime/stage1/models/ced.py. The CED encoder model
code and weights are separate remote assets and retain their own terms.

This isolated route is copied from mizar_l9_12x3_strong_reason. It strictly
inherits the complete official final Mizar checkpoint and retains all 30
physical text layers, executing layers 14-17 four times with shared weights.
Only those four layers train. No gate or other parameters are added.
Online decoding/staging, eight-GPU microbatch-four with up to four-step
gradient accumulation, and complete-state checkpoints retain the reference
training semantics of the complete-AudioMCQ three-epoch reference recipe.
Current source identities are recorded in source_guard_x4.json;
source_guard.json is retained as the historical three-round record.
